+    // A method name may end in `!` as well as `?` — RBS's syntax doc gives
+    // both, and CRuby's method-name rules are the same. Only `?` was
+    // implemented, which was the single largest gap in the top-1000 gem
+    // corpus at 66 files: every `save!`, `clear!` and `use_bundled_cert!`
+    // in the ecosystem.
+    //
+    // The precedence is token-level, not rule-level, and that distinction is
+    // the whole fix for `alias`. `filter!` is a LEXER choice between the
+    // immediate suffix and the `!` operator, which is itself a legal method
+    // name; `?` never had the ambiguity because there is no `?` operator.
+    // Without the token prec, `alias filter! select!` lexes as
+    // `alias filter !` and loses the rest of the line. `alias ! not_op`,
+    // aliasing the operator itself, still parses.
+    identifier_suffix: $ => seq($.identifier, token.immediate(prec(1, choice('?', '!')))),
+    constant_suffix: $ => seq($.constant, token.immediate(prec(1, choice('?', '!')))),
 
     method_name: $ => choice(
       $.identifier,
